{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.common_first_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.common_first_order","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**First-order (frame-invariant) content.** Both frames reduce to `1 + t` modulo `O(t²)`:\ntheir difference vanishes to first order, so the prediction *through* `O(t)` is frame-independent.\nStated as: the linearisations coincide (`Clin` is the common first-order part, and `Cinv − Clin` has\nno constant or linear term — it is `t²·(1/(1−t))`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.g_frame_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.g_frame_difference","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder.lean#L56-L65","doc":"**The bar-even coefficient inherits the `O(t²)` frame difference.** With the bar-even tier\nextracted as `g = (C − 1)/h²` after using bar-odd frame `C`, the two frames differ by\n`(Cinv − Clin)/h² = t²/((1−t) h²)`. Since `t = O(h)`, this is `O(1)` in `h` — the same size as `g`\nitself, so `g` (hence `r = g − 1`) is **not** frame-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.frame_diff_second_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.frame_diff_second_order","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder.lean#L47-L54","doc":"**The two resummations agree at first order and differ at exactly second order:**\n`1/(1−t) − (1+t) = t²/(1−t)`. The frame ambiguity is `O(t²)`, never `O(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.Clin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.Clin","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder.lean#L44-L45","doc":"First-order (additive) form of the bar-odd tier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.Cinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.FrameAmbiguity.Cinv","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/FrameAmbiguitySecondOrder.lean#L41-L42","doc":"Geometric (propagator) resummation of the bar-odd tier. ","signatureChunk":0}]}